[
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm trying to define some syntax as follows:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">module</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">meta</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Parser</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Basic</span>\n<span class=\"n\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">meta</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Parser</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Term</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">namespace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Parser</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Term</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">meta</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">clear?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Parser</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">nonReservedSymbol</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"clear? \"</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">syntax</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inversion</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"s2\">\"inversion \"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"(\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">clear?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\":=\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">trueVal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">falseVal</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\")\"</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ident</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\" with \"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">binderIdent</span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">end</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Parser</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>However, using <code>clear?</code> in the syntax gives the error \"unknown parser declaration/category/alias <code>clear?</code>\", and so does putting <code>(nonReservedSymbol \"clear? \")</code>Am I using parsers wrong here? It seems to have the correct type, e.g. <code>ident</code> is also a <code>Parser</code></p>",
        "id": 600760530,
        "sender_full_name": "Jonathan Chan",
        "timestamp": 1780690827
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Somewhat of a different answer from what you asked, but you probably want to use <code>optConfig</code> here. I'd write:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">syntax</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inversion</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"inversion \"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">optConfig</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\" with\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ppSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">colGt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ident</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hole</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">InversionConfig</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">clear</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bool</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">declare_config_elab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">elabInversionConfig</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">InversionConfig</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The bit at the end will give you a nice elaborator in the tactic monad which works a little nicer than making it from scratch.</p>",
        "id": 600762757,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Henson",
        "timestamp": 1780691808
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>ooh that's nice<br>\nis that documented somewhere?</p>",
        "id": 600763188,
        "sender_full_name": "Jonathan Chan",
        "timestamp": 1780692010
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"407610\">Jonathan Chan</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/239415-metaprogramming-.2F-tactics/topic/.22unknown.20parser.22.20when.20using.20.60nonReservedSymbol.60/near/600760530\">schrieb</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I'm trying to define some syntax as follows:<br>\n...<br>\nHowever, using <code>clear?</code> in the syntax gives the error \"unknown parser declaration/category/alias <code>clear?</code>\", and so does putting <code>(nonReservedSymbol \"clear? \")</code>Am I using parsers wrong here? It seems to have the correct type, e.g. <code>ident</code> is also a <code>Parser</code></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>You forgot <code>public</code>, this works:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">module</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">meta</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Parser</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Basic</span>\n<span class=\"n\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">meta</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Parser</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Term</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">namespace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Parser</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Term</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">meta</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">clear?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Parser</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">nonReservedSymbol</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"clear? \"</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">syntax</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inversion</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"s2\">\"inversion \"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"(\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">clear?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\":=\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">trueVal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">falseVal</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\")\"</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ident</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\" with \"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">binderIdent</span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">end</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Parser</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 600764463,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1780692579
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"407610\">Jonathan Chan</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/239415-metaprogramming-.2F-tactics/topic/.22unknown.20parser.22.20when.20using.20.60nonReservedSymbol.60/near/600763188\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>ooh that's nice<br>\nis that documented somewhere?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>It's very briefly mentioned <a href=\"https://lean-lang.org/doc/reference/latest/Tactic-Proofs/The-Tactic-Language/#tactic-config\">in the reference manual</a>. Syntax wise it'll give <code>inversion +clear with ...</code> and you just use the generated <code>elabInversionConfig</code> to get the corresponding structure from the <code>optConfig</code> syntax.</p>",
        "id": 600764858,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Henson",
        "timestamp": 1780692772
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Note also that for this sort of thing you might find the <code>syntax</code> version convenient: :)</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">syntax</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">clear?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&amp;</span><span class=\"s2\">\"clear? \"</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 600764962,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1780692818
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(But Chris’ approach is indeed the correct one here <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/XY_problem\">#xy</a>-wise <span aria-label=\"grinning face with smiling eyes\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f601\" role=\"img\" title=\"grinning face with smiling eyes\">:grinning_face_with_smiling_eyes:</span>)</p>",
        "id": 600765083,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1780692879
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I can't seem to use the <code>elabInversionConfig</code> in my <code>meta</code> definition <code>evalInversion</code>, am I using it wrong? Or is there a way to mark it as <code>meta</code> when I <code>declare_config_elab</code>?</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Invalid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`meta</span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">definition</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`evalInversion</span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`elabInversionConfig</span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">not</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">marked</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`meta</span><span class=\"bp\">`</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 600806353,
        "sender_full_name": "Jonathan Chan",
        "timestamp": 1780714286
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think it needs to be inside a <code>public meta section</code></p>",
        "id": 600806968,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Henson",
        "timestamp": 1780715039
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>aha that was it! I didn't know about <code>meta section</code>, I might as well just wrap all of my meta stuff in that</p>",
        "id": 600807746,
        "sender_full_name": "Jonathan Chan",
        "timestamp": 1780715841
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>That may be a bug in <code>declare_config_elab</code></p>",
        "id": 600830105,
        "sender_full_name": "Sebastian Ullrich",
        "timestamp": 1780733298
    }
]